Project folder ‘my_brand_assets’ contains brand assets for my product (Logo)
Press enter or click to view image in full size

Project folder ‘my_brand_assets’ contains brand assets for my product (Typography).
After that, you will be able to ask Claude to use this information in design. You can do it in two different ways:

Reference my_brand_assets directory in CLAUDE.md file. For example, you can have a dedicated section called Visual Style where you will provide details on how Claude should use the information in design
## Vistyle Style

When you need company logo for web page use @my_brand_assets/roxy_logo.png
2. Use it in the context of interaction with Claude. You can tag assets right in the Claude prompt field when crafting a design. This approach works well when you’re refining a particular section of the page or UI component.

