Anthropic has recently improved the process of creating new Claude Skills, and this improvement is so significant that it almost feels like Claude Skills 2.0.

In this article, I will share everything you need to know about Claude Skills 2.0, and how your design process can benefit from Claude Skills 2.0

What is Claude Skill
Skill is a built-in mechanism in Claude that gives it reusable capabilities or workflows when it works on particular tasks. Skills help you avoid writing repeated long prompts every time you want Claude to do something for you.

A few examples of Claude Skills that are relevant to the product design space:

PRD writer
Landing page generator
Brand-compliant document creator
API integration workflow
The skill itself is a markdown file (.md) file that contains two things:

YAML frontmatter (between --- markers) that tells Claude when to use the skill
Markdown content with a set of actions that Claude follows when the skill is invoked (typically, it’s a workflow)
SKILL.md

name: design-audit
description: Analyze UI and identify usability problems.

workflow:
1. Review UI screenshot
2. Identify issues
3. Map to UX heuristics
4. Provide redesign suggestions
The great thing about Skills is that they can uplift Claude’s existing capabilities (such as streamlining front-end design and enabling it to create more sophisticated web pages) or guide Claude to follow instructions that are relevant only to your organization.

For example, if your organization follows a particular business process when doing something, you can describe this process as a workflow in your skill and Claude will follow the steps.

Quick note: I have a collection of 10 ready-to-use Claude Skills that you should try as a product designer.

Top 10 Claude Skills You Should Try in Product Design
Claude, Anthropic’s AI assistant, has become one of the most versatile tools in a product designer’s toolkit, capable…
uxplanet.org

Many people explain the role of a skill as a set of instructions that Claude automatically activates for a particular task. While this is a correct way to describe its behavior, it’s better to think of a skill as a recipe.

Just like when we cook something, we rely on a recipe to do the job correctly, Claude will rely on a dedicated skill.

Press enter or click to view image in full size

Recipe for a French toast.
What is Claude Skills 2.0
Claude Skills 2.0 is an informal title for a new tool called Skill-creator. Skill Creator is a meta-skill, a tool that automatically generates new Claude Skills for you.

Press enter or click to view image in full size

Skill-creator in Anthropic repository (Source link)
Instead of manually writing a skill from scratch and placing it in a SKILL.md file, you can simply describe the capability you want in plain language, and Skill Creator will:

Analyze the requested capability
Ask clarifying questions
Design the skill architecture
Generate the full skill package
The great thing about Skill Creator is that it triggers a process that evaluates the quality of output a newly created skill will produce. This evaluation is exactly what helps you achieve better results with your skill.

Creating a new front-end skill in 4 simple steps
To illustrate how Skill Creator works, I will create a new front-end design Claude Skill using this tool. I will do it in VSCode with Claude Code integration.

Step 1: Install ‘skill-creator’
I will open an empty directory on my local machine and run Claude Code.

Press enter or click to view image in full size

Claude Code view in VSCode.
The first thing I need to do is install skill-creator. To do that, I will need to type a command:

/manage plugins
Press enter or click to view image in full size

Type a command ‘/manage plugins’ in Claude
Next, I need to search for skill-creator and click Install.

Press enter or click to view image in full size

Installing ‘skill-creator’ for your Claude.
Claude will offer a few options for plugin installation. I suggest choosing “Install for you”, because it will make skill-creator available across all projects you work on your local machine.

Press enter or click to view image in full size

‘Install for you’ means that skill-creator will be available in all Claude project.
Once you install the skill-creator, you need to restart the Claude session. And I also recommend you submit a prompt.

Do you have skill-creator available for crafting new skills?
Press enter or click to view image in full size

Make sure we have ‘skill-creator’ available for our task.
Step 2: Prompt Claude to create a new skill
Now that we know that we have skill-creator, we can use it to build a new skill. I will create a front-end web design skill that will craft a landing page in the style of Apple products.

To do that, I will prompt Claude:

I want to create a new skill called super-landing-page that will take the page
requirements as input, analyze them, identify gaps and missing information,
and ask me clarifying questions. After that, it will use this information
to code a modern, sophisticated landing page design in the style of Apple.
Press enter or click to view image in full size

Asking Claude to create a new skill called ‘super-landing-page’
I want to highlight 3 important things about this prompt:

Skill name. I give the skill the name “super-landing-page.” I will use this name when I ask Claude to use it for my design.
Workflow. I explain how the skill should work (what input I will provide, what Claude should do with it, and what I expect the skill to build using this information).
Ultimate goal. I want the skill to create not just a generic page, but a page in the style of Apple products.
Once I submit this prompt, Claude will create a to-do list of steps that it will follow to build the skill. Notice that one of the steps is “create test cases in evals.” This is where the skill evaluates the quality of the output it produces.

Press enter or click to view image in full size

To do plan created by skill-created for a new skill.
Step 3: Skill-creator builds a new skill
This step is done by skill-creator with minimal involvement from you.

During this step, skill-creator will:

Draft a new skill
Test it with a few inputs
Analyze the quality of outputs produced by the skill
At the end of this process, you will see a results table. This table lists results with and without the skill, and you can see that skill-creator helped improve the quality of the output produced by super-landing-page (in this case, the front-end design generated for our landing page).

Press enter or click to view image in full size

Quality of output generated by super-landing-page skill (with skill and without skill).
